{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat report.md; cat analysis/group_analysis.py; cat input/upstream-methods.md; cat results/summary.json; cat results/run.log'","aggregated_output":".bashrc sourced.\n.bash_profile sourced\n# Potential gains and vmPFC activity in the NARPS equal-indifference group\n\n## Result\n\n**The supplied group maps do not support a positive gain effect in vmPFC under whole-brain corrected inference.** Across all 54 participants, the mean effect in an independently specified vmPFC core mask was 0.0018 contrast units (between-participant SD 0.0629; 95% t interval −0.0153 to 0.0190; one-sided uncorrected *p* = .416). The interval includes zero and effects in either direction; this is not an equivalence test.\n\nA one-sided whole-brain max-*T* permutation test did identify 23 significant voxels (*p*FWE ≤ .05), with the strongest at MNI (−26, −102, −3.6), *t*(53) = 6.62, *p*FWE = .0009. This is posterior left occipital cortex, not vmPFC, and does not support the stated regional hypothesis. The small non-target finding should be interpreted cautiously; it is a whole-brain result, not an independently replicated effect.\n\n![Positive voxels surviving one-sided whole-brain max-T family-wise error correction](figures/whole_brain_fwe_findings.png)\n\nThe uncorrected group map is shown for anatomical context only. Its display threshold (*p* < .001 uncorrected) is not the inferential threshold.\n\n![Uncorrected group t map and vmPFC view](figures/group_t_map.png)\n\n## Analysis\n\nThe 54 AO86 participant gain contrast estimates (COPEs) were tested with an equal-weight one-sample random-effects *t* model against zero (*df* = 53). Each value is an upstream participant-level contrast estimate—not a *t*/*z* statistic. An independently specified vmPFC core envelope (MNI x = −15 to 15, y = 20 to 55, z = −20 to 5 mm) was used to summarize the target-region estimate and its uncertainty. This broad anatomical summary is descriptive; the confirmatory search was whole brain, consistent with the [original NARPS analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf), which require whole-brain corrected evidence for the named region.\n\nThe primary inference used 9,999 random sign flips of participant effects and the maximum positive *t* statistic across the analysis mask on each permutation, controlling voxelwise family-wise error at .05. The analysis mask was the intersection of a standard MNI brain mask and nonzero locations across all 54 maps. The latter avoids treating zeros outside individual estimation support as observed zero effects. It contains 186,400 voxels; 2,687 fall in the vmPFC core. All maps had the same 97 × 115 × 81 grid, 2 × 2 × 2.4 mm voxel spacing and affine; all 54 participant IDs matched metadata. No participants were excluded. The full group *t* map, max-*T* adjusted *p* map, thresholded significant *t* map, JSON summary and run log are in `results/`.\n\n![Participant vmPFC-core mean effects and group interval](figures/vmPFC_participant_effects.png)\n\n## Interpretation and limits\n\nA lack of corrected vmPFC support means this analysis did not detect evidence strong enough to pass whole-brain family-wise error control in that region. It does **not** show that the true effect is zero or rule out a smaller effect; the descriptive interval remains compatible with positive and negative effects.\n\nThe gain modulator was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution. Thus, the supplied coefficient is not a response change per currency unit. Response-time duration, choice regressors, motion, flagged volumes and drift were included upstream, while gain and loss were modeled separately; the estimate is conditional on those fixed choices. Because participant variance maps and an executable upstream model are unavailable, the group test gives participants equal weight and cannot account for differing first-level precision. Sign-flip inference also assumes participant effects are exchangeable and null errors are symmetric. The common-support mask excludes locations not estimated for every participant. The analysis tests the supplied contrast in this group; it does not establish causality or directly compare the gain and loss range manipulation.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nRun `analysis/group_analysis.py` with the supplied Python environment. Outputs are written to `results/` and `figures/`; numeric results are in `results/summary.json`. Inputs and fixed modeling details are documented in `input/sources.json` and `input/upstream-methods.md`.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Group inference for NARPS Hypothesis 1, AO86 equal-indifference gain cope maps.\n\nPrimary: one-sample random-effects t test with one-sided whole-brain max-T\nsign-flip permutation FWE correction. No first-level variance maps are supplied,\nso participants receive equal weight. All randomization and masks are deterministic.\n\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport hashlib\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport nibabel as nib\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom nilearn import datasets, image, plotting\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nOUT = ROOT / \"results\"\nFIG = ROOT / \"figures\"\nDATA = ROOT / \"input\" / \"data\"\nN_PERM = 9999\nSEED = 8601\nALPHA = .05\n\nmeta = pd.read_csv(ROOT / \"input\" / \"participants.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\")\nfiles = sorted(DATA.glob(\"sub-*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\"))\nfile_ids = [p.name.split(\"_\")[0] for p in files]\nassert len(files) == 54 and set(file_ids) == set(meta.participant_id)\nmeta = meta.set_index(\"participant_id\").loc[file_ids].reset_index()\nimgs = [nib.load(str(p)) for p in files]\nref = imgs[0]\nfor p, im in zip(files, imgs):\n    assert im.shape == ref.shape, f\"shape mismatch: {p.name}\"\n    assert np.allclose(im.affine, ref.affine, atol=1e-5), f\"affine mismatch: {p.name}\"\n\n# An independent standard MNI brain mask, nearest-neighbor resampled to the\n# supplied MNI152NLin2009cAsym grid. Positive-coverage voxels inside brain only.\nstd_mask = datasets.load_mni152_brain_mask(resolution=2)\nmask_img = image.resample_to_img(std_mask, ref, interpolation=\"nearest\", force_resample=True)\nbrain = np.asarray(mask_img.dataobj) > 0\nYvol = np.stack([np.asarray(im.dataobj, dtype=np.float32) for im in imgs], axis=0)\nfinite = np.isfinite(Yvol).all(axis=0)\n# NIfTI zeros mark locations outside each participant's estimation mask in this\n# collection. Use their intersection so no fabricated zero observations enter\n# the group test; an exactly zero floating-point contrast throughout all maps\n# is vanishingly unlikely.\ncoverage = np.all(Yvol != 0, axis=0)\nmask = brain & finite & coverage\nassert mask.sum() > 50000\nY = Yvol[:, mask].astype(np.float64, copy=False)\nn, v = Y.shape\n\n# One-sample t and one-sided parametric p maps for descriptive comparison.\nmean = Y.mean(axis=0)\nsd = Y.std(axis=0, ddof=1)\ntobs = mean / (sd / np.sqrt(n))\np_unc = stats.t.sf(tobs, df=n-1)\n\n# Sign-flip randomization under the null of symmetric participant effects.\n# For each sign vector, calculate all voxel statistics and retain its maximum.\nrng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\nmax_t = np.empty(N_PERM, dtype=np.float64)\nsumsq = np.einsum(\"ij,ij->j\", Y, Y)\nbatch = 64\nfor start in range(0, N_PERM, batch):\n    b = min(batch, N_PERM-start)\n    signs = rng.choice(np.array([-1., 1.]), size=(b, n))\n    sums = signs @ Y\n    denom2 = (sumsq[None, :] - sums*sums/n) / (n-1)\n    ts = (sums / n) / np.sqrt(np.maximum(denom2, 1e-30) / n)\n    max_t[start:start+b] = np.max(ts, axis=1)\np_fwe = (1 + (max_t[:, None] >= tobs[None, :]).sum(axis=0)) / (N_PERM + 1)\n\n# Convert maps back to reference image space.\ndef out_img(vals):\n    arr = np.zeros(ref.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    arr[mask] = np.asarray(vals, dtype=np.float32)\n    return nib.Nifti1Image(arr, ref.affine, ref.header)\nt_img = out_img(tobs)\np_img = out_img(p_fwe)\nmean_img = out_img(mean)\nfor name, im in [(\"mean_gain_effect.nii.gz\", mean_img), (\"t_statistic.nii.gz\", t_img), (\"p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz\", p_img)]:\n    nib.save(im, OUT / name)\n\n# A fixed, broad anatomical vmPFC core envelope in MNI coordinates, used only\n# for an interpretable descriptive summary. Inference remains whole-brain.\nijk = np.indices(ref.shape).reshape(3, -1).T\nxyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, ijk)\nroi_flat = ((np.abs(xyz[:,0]) <= 15) & (xyz[:,1] >= 20) & (xyz[:,1] <= 55) &\n            (xyz[:,2] >= -20) & (xyz[:,2] <= 5))\nroi = roi_flat.reshape(ref.shape) & mask\nassert roi.sum() > 20\nroi_vals = Yvol[:, roi]\nsubj_roi = roi_vals.mean(axis=1)\nroi_mean = subj_roi.mean()\nroi_sd = subj_roi.std(ddof=1)\nroi_se = roi_sd / np.sqrt(n)\nroi_ci = stats.t.interval(.95, n-1, loc=roi_mean, scale=roi_se)\nroi_t = roi_mean / roi_se\nroi_p = stats.t.sf(roi_t, n-1)\n\n# Peak and cluster-like extent in max-T FWE-significant voxels (voxelwise FWE).\nsig = p_fwe <= ALPHA\nsig_count = int(sig.sum())\nsig_t_img = out_img(np.where(sig, tobs, 0.0))\nnib.save(sig_t_img, OUT / \"t_fwe_significant.nii.gz\")\npeak_idx = None\nif sig_count:\n    peak_local = np.argmax(np.where(sig, tobs, -np.inf))\n    peak_idx = np.argwhere(mask)[peak_local]\n    peak_xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, peak_idx)\n    peak_t = float(tobs[peak_local]); peak_pfwe = float(p_fwe[peak_local])\nelse:\n    peak_xyz = None; peak_t = None; peak_pfwe = None\n\n# QC metrics and checks.\nnonzero_frac = np.mean(Yvol != 0, axis=(1,2,3))\nsubj_whole_mean = Y.mean(axis=1)\nqc = {\n  \"n_maps\": len(files), \"n_metadata\": len(meta), \"all_metadata_ids_matched\": True,\n  \"excluded_participants\": [], \"common_grid_shape\": list(ref.shape),\n  \"voxel_sizes_mm\": [float(x) for x in ref.header.get_zooms()[:3]],\n  \"reference_affine\": ref.affine.tolist(), \"whole_brain_mask_voxels\": int(mask.sum()),\n  \"vmPFC_core_mask_voxels\": int(roi.sum()), \"map_nonzero_fraction_range\": [float(nonzero_frac.min()), float(nonzero_frac.max())],\n  \"participant_whole_brain_mean_range\": [float(subj_whole_mean.min()), float(subj_whole_mean.max())],\n  \"participant_vmPFC_mean_range\": [float(subj_roi.min()), float(subj_roi.max())]\n}\nsummary = {\n  \"analysis\": \"one-sample equal-weight random-effects t test; positive gain effect\",\n  \"n\": n, \"df\": n-1, \"mask_voxels\": v, \"permutations\": N_PERM,\n  \"permutation_seed\": SEED, \"test\": \"one-sided sign-flip max-T voxelwise family-wise error control\",\n  \"alpha\": ALPHA, \"vmPFC_roi_definition_mni_mm\": {\"x\": [-15,15], \"y\": [20,55], \"z\": [-20,5]},\n  \"vmPFC_roi_role\": \"descriptive summary only; confirmatory inference uses full brain mask\",\n  \"vmPFC_roi_mean_effect\": float(roi_mean), \"vmPFC_roi_sd_between_participants\": float(roi_sd),\n  \"vmPFC_roi_se\": float(roi_se), \"vmPFC_roi_95ci\": [float(roi_ci[0]), float(roi_ci[1])],\n  \"vmPFC_roi_t\": float(roi_t), \"vmPFC_roi_uncorrected_one_sided_p\": float(roi_p),\n  \"whole_brain_maxT_fwe_significant_voxels\": sig_count,\n  \"peak_if_significant_mni_mm\": None if peak_xyz is None else [float(q) for q in peak_xyz],\n  \"peak_t\": peak_t, \"peak_p_fwe\": peak_pfwe,\n  \"most_extreme_wholebrain_t\": float(tobs.max()), \"most_extreme_wholebrain_mni_mm\": [float(q) for q in nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, np.argwhere(mask)[np.argmax(tobs)])],\n  \"maxT_95pct_critical_t\": float(np.quantile(max_t, .95)),\n  \"n_voxels_uncorrected_p_lt_0_001\": int((p_unc < .001).sum()),\n  \"qc\": qc\n}\n(OUT / \"summary.json\").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n# Figure 1: group t statistic on sagittal and coronal slices, with vmPFC envelope outline.\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4.5))\nplotting.plot_stat_map(t_img, bg_img=datasets.load_mni152_template(resolution=2),\n    display_mode=\"x\", cut_coords=[0], threshold=stats.t.ppf(.999, n-1),\n    cmap=\"cold_hot\", colorbar=True, vmax=max(4, float(np.nanpercentile(tobs,99.9))),\n    axes=axes[0], title=\"Group t map (display threshold p < .001 uncorrected)\")\nplotting.plot_stat_map(t_img, bg_img=datasets.load_mni152_template(resolution=2),\n    display_mode=\"y\", cut_coords=[35], threshold=stats.t.ppf(.999, n-1),\n    cmap=\"cold_hot\", colorbar=True, vmax=max(4, float(np.nanpercentile(tobs,99.9))),\n    axes=axes[1], title=\"Coronal view through vmPFC\")\nfig.suptitle(\"NARPS equal-indifference gain effect (n=54)\", fontsize=13)\nfig.tight_layout()\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"group_t_map.png\", dpi=180, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\nplt.close(fig)\n\n# Corrected whole-brain findings, plotted at the peak and vmPFC midsagittal plane.\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(12, 4.2))\nfor ax, mode, coord, title in [\n    (axes[0], \"x\", -26, \"Sagittal: peak x = -26\"),\n    (axes[1], \"y\", -102, \"Coronal: peak y = -102\"),\n    (axes[2], \"z\", -4, \"Axial: peak z = -4\"),\n]:\n    plotting.plot_stat_map(sig_t_img, bg_img=datasets.load_mni152_template(resolution=2),\n        display_mode=mode, cut_coords=[coord], threshold=0, cmap=\"cold_hot\",\n        colorbar=True, axes=ax, title=title)\nfig.suptitle(\"Positive voxels surviving one-sided whole-brain max-T FWE (p ≤ .05)\", fontsize=12)\nfig.tight_layout()\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"whole_brain_fwe_findings.png\", dpi=180, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\nplt.close(fig)\n\n# Figure 2: participant vmPFC ROI effect distribution and group estimate.\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4.5))\nax.scatter(np.arange(1,n+1), subj_roi, s=24, color=\"#345995\", alpha=.8)\nax.axhline(roi_mean, color=\"#c44536\", lw=2, label=f\"Mean = {roi_mean:.3f}\")\nax.axhspan(roi_ci[0], roi_ci[1], color=\"#c44536\", alpha=.15, label=\"95% t interval\")\nax.axhline(0, color=\"black\", lw=.8)\nax.set(xlabel=\"Participant (ordered by ID)\", ylabel=\"Mean gain contrast estimate in vmPFC core\", title=\"Participant-level vmPFC gain effect\")\nax.legend(frameon=False); fig.tight_layout()\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"vmPFC_participant_effects.png\", dpi=180, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\nplt.close(fig)\n\nprint(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n{\n  \"analysis\": \"one-sample equal-weight random-effects t test; positive gain effect\",\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"df\": 53,\n  \"mask_voxels\": 186400,\n  \"permutations\": 9999,\n  \"permutation_seed\": 8601,\n  \"test\": \"one-sided sign-flip max-T voxelwise family-wise error control\",\n  \"alpha\": 0.05,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_definition_mni_mm\": {\n    \"x\": [\n      -15,\n      15\n    ],\n    \"y\": [\n      20,\n      55\n    ],\n    \"z\": [\n      -20,\n      5\n    ]\n  },\n  \"vmPFC_roi_role\": \"descriptive summary only; confirmatory inference uses full brain mask\",\n  \"vmPFC_roi_mean_effect\": 0.001825780258513987,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_sd_between_participants\": 0.06288476288318634,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_se\": 0.008557532314428736,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_95ci\": [\n    -0.015338455910954701,\n    0.018990016427982676\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_roi_t\": 0.21335359206713883,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_uncorrected_one_sided_p\": 0.41593488480667573,\n  \"whole_brain_maxT_fwe_significant_voxels\": 23,\n  \"peak_if_significant_mni_mm\": [\n    -26.0,\n    -102.0,\n    -3.599997043609619\n  ],\n  \"peak_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n  \"peak_p_fwe\": 0.0009,\n  \"most_extreme_wholebrain_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n  \"most_extreme_wholebrain_mni_mm\": [\n    -26.0,\n    -102.0,\n    -3.599997043609619\n  ],\n  \"maxT_95pct_critical_t\": 5.354057819855591,\n  \"n_voxels_uncorrected_p_lt_0_001\": 599,\n  \"qc\": {\n    \"n_maps\": 54,\n    \"n_metadata\": 54,\n    \"all_metadata_ids_matched\": true,\n    \"excluded_participants\": [],\n    \"common_grid_shape\": [\n      97,\n      115,\n      81\n    ],\n    \"voxel_sizes_mm\": [\n      2.0,\n      2.0,\n      2.4000000953674316\n    ],\n    \"reference_affine\": [\n      [\n        2.0,\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        -96.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        2.0,\n        0.0,\n        -132.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        2.4000000953674316,\n        -78.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        1.0\n      ]\n    ],\n    \"whole_brain_mask_voxels\": 186400,\n    \"vmPFC_core_mask_voxels\": 2687,\n    \"map_nonzero_fraction_range\": [\n      0.24085418153847857,\n      0.25719519011017594\n    ],\n    \"participant_whole_brain_mean_range\": [\n      -0.1264558371855069,\n      0.10149091513023888\n    ],\n    \"participant_vmPFC_mean_range\": [\n      -0.1162855327129364,\n      0.19704456627368927\n    ]\n  }\n}\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-01/analysis/group_analysis.py:159: UserWarning: This figure includes Axes that are not compatible with tight_layout, so results might be incorrect.\n  fig.tight_layout()\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-01/analysis/group_analysis.py:174: UserWarning: This figure includes Axes that are not compatible with tight_layout, so results might be incorrect.\n  fig.tight_layout()\n{\n  \"analysis\": \"one-sample equal-weight random-effects t test; positive gain effect\",\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"df\": 53,\n  \"mask_voxels\": 186400,\n  \"permutations\": 9999,\n  \"permutation_seed\": 8601,\n  \"test\": \"one-sided sign-flip max-T voxelwise family-wise error control\",\n  \"alpha\": 0.05,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_definition_mni_mm\": {\n    \"x\": [\n      -15,\n      15\n    ],\n    \"y\": [\n      20,\n      55\n    ],\n    \"z\": [\n      -20,\n      5\n    ]\n  },\n  \"vmPFC_roi_role\": \"descriptive summary only; confirmatory inference uses full brain mask\",\n  \"vmPFC_roi_mean_effect\": 0.001825780258513987,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_sd_between_participants\": 0.06288476288318634,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_se\": 0.008557532314428736,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_95ci\": [\n    -0.015338455910954701,\n    0.018990016427982676\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_roi_t\": 0.21335359206713883,\n  \"vmPFC_roi_uncorrected_one_sided_p\": 0.41593488480667573,\n  \"whole_brain_maxT_fwe_significant_voxels\": 23,\n  \"peak_if_significant_mni_mm\": [\n    -26.0,\n    -102.0,\n    -3.599997043609619\n  ],\n  \"peak_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n  \"peak_p_fwe\": 0.0009,\n  \"most_extreme_wholebrain_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n  \"most_extreme_wholebrain_mni_mm\": [\n    -26.0,\n    -102.0,\n    -3.599997043609619\n  ],\n  \"maxT_95pct_critical_t\": 5.354057819855591,\n  \"n_voxels_uncorrected_p_lt_0_001\": 599,\n  \"qc\": {\n    \"n_maps\": 54,\n    \"n_metadata\": 54,\n    \"all_metadata_ids_matched\": true,\n    \"excluded_participants\": [],\n    \"common_grid_shape\": [\n      97,\n      115,\n      81\n    ],\n    \"voxel_sizes_mm\": [\n      2.0,\n      2.0,\n      2.4000000953674316\n    ],\n    \"reference_affine\": [\n      [\n        2.0,\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        -96.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        2.0,\n        0.0,\n        -132.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        2.4000000953674316,\n        -78.0\n      ],\n      [\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        0.0,\n        1.0\n      ]\n    ],\n    \"whole_brain_mask_voxels\": 186400,\n    \"vmPFC_core_mask_voxels\": 2687,\n    \"map_nonzero_fraction_range\": [\n      0.24085418153847857,\n      0.25719519011017594\n    ],\n    \"participant_whole_brain_mean_range\": [\n      -0.1264558371855069,\n      0.10149091513023888\n    ],\n    \"participant_vmPFC_mean_range\": [\n      -0.1162855327129364,\n      0.19704456627368927\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
