amped-checklist:may/005: value None does not follow from status 'partial'\nrefusing to encode an invalid response; pass --allow-invalid to override\n| item | principles | status | source | evidence | reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| must/001 | S.1 | met | judgement | `report.md`, `input/participants.tsv` | The complete project is arranged under one workspace root. |\n| must/002 | S.1 | met | judgement | `input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz`, `input/sources.json` | The supplied data links resolve within the project root to retained annex content. |\n| must/003 | S.1 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | External software dependencies are not included in an environment or linked submodule. |\n| must/004 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py`, `report.md` | At worker stop Git contains supplied inputs, while the analysis, report, figures and results are outside the captured commit. |\n| must/005 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | met | judgement | `input/data/` | All 54 large participant maps are represented by annex pointers with retained content. |\n| must/006 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | unmet | judgement | `results/run.log`, `analysis/group_analysis.py` | The run log records output but does not identify an exact environment that produced the results. |\n| must/007 | A.1 | unmet | judgement | `report.md` | The report gives a command, but no README or Makefile provides installation and usage instructions. |\n| must/008 | A.1 | met | judgement | `report.md`, `analysis/group_analysis.py` | The report documents analysis/group_analysis.py as a starting point and gives its execution command. |\n| must/009 | P.1 | met | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | The analysis uses paths relative to its own file location. |\n| must/010 | P.1 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | The imported software dependencies are not declared in an environment specification. |\n| must/011 | P.1 | unmet | judgement | `report.md`, `.git/config` | The report does not document host or system assumptions; captured Git config also points hooks to an absolute host path. |\n| must/012 | P.2 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No README or environment specification lists system requirements and dependencies. |\n| must/013 | P.3 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No environment specification is included in the captured version control state. |\n| must/014 | P.3 | unmet | judgement | `report.md` | No process for updating or tracking environment specifications is documented. |\n| must/015 | D.1 | unmet | judgement | `results/run.log` | No pinned environment specification is supplied for exact reconstruction. |\n| must/016 | D.1 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No environment specification is supplied for sharing. |\n| must/017 | D.1 | unmet | judgement | `report.md` | The report gives no route to obtain or use a reproducible environment specification. |\n| should/001 | T.2 | partial | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py`, `input/data/` | Git and git-annex cover supplied inputs, but the worker's scientific code, report and outputs are outside the captured commit. |\n| should/002 | A.2 | unmet | judgement | `results/run.log` | The stop state contains one analysis run and no recurring workflow test process. |\n| should/003 | M.1 | partial | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py`, `report.md` | Inputs, code, results and figures have separate directories, but no distinct environment module is supplied. |\n| should/004 | E.1 | unmet | judgement | `results/run.log` | No worker evidence shows routine execution in a fresh container, batch job, VM or cloud instance. |\n| should/005 | E.1 | unmet | judgement | `report.md` | No disposable per-run environment mechanism is documented or captured. |\n| should/006 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `results/run.log` | There is no exact environment specification to test for reconstruction. |\n| should/007 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No environment artifact is archived with the project. |\n| should/008 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `report.md` | No environment specification update process is documented. |\n| should/009 | M.4 | not-applicable | judgement | `input/sources.json` | The supplied analysis object contains no identified restricted data or software module. |\n| may/001 | M.2 | not-applicable | judgement | `input/data/` | No independently maintained project component is included as a submodule; the participant data are vendored through annex. |\n| may/002 | M.2 | partial | judgement | `report.md` | The report identifies inputs, analysis source, results and figures, but does not document a modular composition model. |\n| may/003 | M.2 | not-applicable | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No independently composable project modules are defined. |\n| may/004 | M.2 | not-applicable | judgement | `analysis/group_analysis.py` | No separate modules require a composition mechanism. |\n| may/005 | M.2 | partial | judgement | `report.md` | The report points readers to the analysis script and results but there is no navigation or module guide. |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=\\\"response.json\\\"; r=json.load(open(p))\nr[\\\"assessor\\\"][\\\"model\\\"]=\\\"not recorded by runtime\\\"\nr[\\\"assessor\\\"][\\\"dependencies\\\"]=[\\\"stamped-conventions@0.1.0\\\"]\nfor item in r[\\\"responses\\\"].values():\n s=item[\\\"status\\\"]\n item[\\\"value\\\"]=\\\"yes\\\" if s==\\\"met\\\" else \\\"no\\\" if s in (\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"partial\\\") else None\njson.dump(r,open(p,\\\"w\\\"),indent=2);open(p,\\\"a\\\").write(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response validate response.json\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode response.json > checklist-link.txt\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
