e are asserted; and the intersection of nonzero coverage avoids treating outside-estimation zeros as data. The reported MNI vmPFC envelope is explicit and used descriptively while confirmatory inference remains whole brain, as required. Fixed upstream mean-centered, variance-normalized gain estimates are not currency-unit response slopes, and participant variance maps are unavailable; equal weighting and the report's stated symmetric/exchangeable sign-flip assumption therefore limit interpretation. The output also does not directly compare gain and loss or establish causality. These qualifications do not overturn the reported absence of corrected vmPFC support. No replay result is used as scientific evidence.\n    10\t\n    11\tEvidence: analysis/group_analysis.py (SHA-256 9b4df616e47890d4236a96b7cd7359ef58a91aa5f42968a17bcf9e516af1f6d2), results/summary.json (4cc200c8c6dd21e8cad9fbe9d9f8a8177487198c5666106082322ec8564b1fd0), report.md (8e70ad20b717ded5ab34a9cebf741da55fbd6d381dc3f51041376719bce82a14), input/upstream-methods.md (508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b), and input/participants.tsv (faca815bcb042144bdb8dcff915f45de0d27650f60416ed76a5a72557341abbf). Each path refers to bytes in the canonical capture named above.\n    12\t\n    13\tThe code checks map geometry and cohort membership, but the written QC does not show participant overlay or coverage visualizations; the plotted group maps help inspect the group result but do not fully substitute for per-map spatial QC. Inference is bounded to common support and the chosen anatomical envelope. The supplied upstream methods also state that no first-level variance maps or executable upstream model are available.\n    14\t\n    15\t**Reported hypothesis outcome:** no positive vmPFC gain effect is supported under whole-brain correction. This is the worker's reported outcome, kept separate from scientific adequacy.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Replay and measurement availability\n    18\t\n    19\tReplay is **not checked**. Before replay, the declared command was python analysis/group_analysis.py; prerequisites were the captured inputs and the worker-described “supplied Python environment,” with no added dependency installation or repair. The selected generated outputs were the four named NIfTI maps, results/summary.json, and the three named figures. The declared comparison was numeric table comparison at rtol=1e-6; images would be byte-compared; logs, timestamps and prose were not selected as scientific outputs.\n    20\t\n    21\tThe first frozen-helper invocation failed before materialization because I had created its required-new work directory. I preserved its command, stdout, stderr and exit status under replay/. A second invocation was refused with “Formal replay allowance already consumed”; no scientific entrypoint ran. This is an assessor invocation/setup failure, not target behavior. No replacement replay was attempted. See replay/replay-record.json and the two retained command/output sets.\n    22\t\n    23\t## STAMPED assessment\n    24\t\n    25\t| Level | Met | Partial | Unmet | Not checked | Not applicable |\n    26\t|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n    27\t| MUST | 5 | 0 | 12 | 0 | 0 |\n    28\t| SHOULD | 0 | 2 | 6 | 0 | 1 |\n408d85105861831de293307e42dfbaaf471e3fc6cd8bb211606b8c3401dbe41d  2026-10-16-assessment.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
